  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Amplifying Voices, Improving Services: Youth and Disability-Led Social Accountability in Yeka Sub City, Addis Ababa.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &#x2018;Amplifying Voices, Improving Services: Youth and Disability-Led Social Accountability in Yeka Sub City, Addis Ababa&#x2019; aims to contribute to the quality and equity of public service delivery in Yeka Sub-City by reducing systemic barriers to inclusion and establishing a sustainable, youth- and disability-led social accountability ecosystem that compels responsive and transparent governance through: (1) Building a foundational cohort of 1,000 empowered youth advocates on rights, and practical skills to reduce service gaps, through awareness creation, enhanced knowledge, utilizing SA tools, and articulating evidence-based demands to duty-bearers; (2) Establishing evidence-based, participatory feedback mechanisms targeting and empowering 200 government officials and service providers (50% females); and (3) Co-create/operationalize 10 permanent, and accessible platforms for inclusive dialogue and decision making in the 5 targeted Woredas.</narrative>
  </description>
